#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md:37
msgid ""
"Comparison-related methods. If a type implements `PartialOrd`/`Ord` then you "
"can use comparison operators (`<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`) with that type."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md:40
msgid "`Ord` gives access to `min`, `max`, and `clamp` methods."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md:42
msgid "When derived, compares things in the order they are defined."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md:44
msgid ""
"For enums this means each variant is considered \"greater than\" the last as "
"they are written."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md:47
msgid ""
"For structs this means fields are compared as they are written, so `id` "
"fields are compared before `name` fields in `Totally`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md:50
msgid "Prerequisites: `PartialEq` for `PartialOrd`, `Eq` for `Ord`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md:52
msgid ""
"To implement `Ord`, a type must also implement `PartialEq`, `Eq`, and "
"`PartialOrd`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md:55
msgid ""
"Like with `PartialEq` and `Eq`, a type cannot implement `Ord` without "
"implementing `PartialOrd`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md:58
msgid ""
"Like those equality traits, `PartialOrd` exists to separate types with non-"
"total ordering (particularly floating-point numbers) from types with total "
"ordering."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md:62
msgid ""
"Used for sorting/searching algorithms and maintaining the ordering of "
"`BTreeMap`/`BTreeSet` style data types."
msgstr ""
